#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:121
msgid ""
"We set the node's flow limit in ``global`` and the HTTP request allowance "
"in ``http``. The ``plugins`` map names the checks. Each frontend chooses "
"which checks run. The two threads in ``hook_judges`` handle "
"connection-stage agent calls, with room for 64 waiting connections. The "
"console keeps its accounts and audit records in its own SQLite directory."
msgstr ""
"En ``global`` fijamos el límite de flujos del nodo y en ``http`` la cuota "
"de peticiones HTTP. El mapa ``plugins`` da nombre a los controles. Cada "
"frontend selecciona cuáles se ejecutan. Los dos hilos de ``hook_judges`` "
"consultan al agente en la fase de conexión y admiten hasta 64 conexiones "
"en espera. La consola guarda las cuentas y los registros de auditoría en "
"su propio directorio SQLite."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:123
msgid ""
"The value of ``http.policy_file`` names a JSON file. We save this policy "
"as ``policy.json`` beside the module. It challenges requests by default "
"and denies requests for the retired timetable. We run the commands from "
"that directory so the relative paths resolve."
msgstr ""
"El valor de ``http.policy_file`` nombra un archivo JSON. Guardamos esta "
"política como ``policy.json`` junto al módulo. Por defecto presenta un "
"desafío y deniega las peticiones del horario retirado. Ejecutamos las "
"órdenes desde ese directorio para que se resuelvan las rutas relativas."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:125
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"default_action\": \"CHALLENGE\",\n"
"  \"rules\": [{ \"name\": \"retired\", \"path\": \"/retired/*\", "
"\"action\": \"DENY\" }]\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"{\n"
"  \"default_action\": \"CHALLENGE\",\n"
"  \"rules\": [{ \"name\": \"retired\", \"path\": \"/retired/*\", "
"\"action\": \"DENY\" }]\n"
"}"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:132
msgid ""
"(umask 077 && openssl rand 32 > http.key)\n"
"mkdir -p console-data\n"
"sibuna init-admin admin --data-dir console-data\n"
"sibuna check -f station.jlv\n"
"sibuna --config-file station.jlv"
msgstr ""
"(umask 077 && openssl rand 32 > http.key)\n"
"mkdir -p console-data\n"
"sibuna init-admin admin --data-dir console-data\n"
"sibuna check -f station.jlv\n"
"sibuna --config-file station.jlv"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:140
msgid ""
"We create the seed and administrator once. Each replica must answer ``GET "
"/healthz`` and the staff agent must listen on ``staff.sock`` before it "
"can admit staff connections. With Sibuna running, we can check readiness, "
"inspect the pool and sign in at ``http://127.0.0.1:9443/console/``."
msgstr ""
"Creamos una sola vez la semilla y la cuenta de administración. Cada "
"réplica debe responder a ``GET /healthz`` y el agente del personal debe "
"escuchar en ``staff.sock`` para admitir conexiones. Con Sibuna en marcha, "
"podemos comprobar si está listo, consultar el grupo e iniciar sesión en "
"``http://127.0.0.1:9443/console/``."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:142
msgid ""
"curl http://127.0.0.1:9100/ready\n"
"sibuna ctl edge.sock show servers\n"
"sibuna ctl edge.sock show hooks"
msgstr ""
"curl http://127.0.0.1:9100/ready\n"
"sibuna ctl edge.sock show servers\n"
"sibuna ctl edge.sock show hooks"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:148
msgid "Route a browser and an RPC client"
msgstr "Enrutar un navegador y un cliente RPC"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:151
msgid ""
"This module uses a typed helper to name an origin. The public portal uses "
"the shield. Calls under ``/orders.Orders/`` use an HTTP/2 pool and skip "
"the browser firewall. The RPC service must authenticate its callers."
msgstr ""
"Este módulo usa una función auxiliar tipada para nombrar un servidor de "
"origen. El portal público usa el escudo. Las llamadas bajo "
"``/orders.Orders/`` usan un grupo HTTP/2 y omiten el cortafuegos del "
"navegador. El servicio RPC debe autenticar a quienes lo llaman."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:153
msgid ""
"fn service(name: Text, address: Text) -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return { name: name, addr: address }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return {\n"
"        global: { acme: { storage: \"certificates\", directory: "
"\"letsencrypt-staging\" } },\n"
"        http: { surface: \"shield\" },\n"
"        frontends: { https: {\n"
"            binds: [\"0.0.0.0:443\"],\n"
"            tls: { auto: [\"portal.example.org\", \"orders.internal\"], "
"http3: true },\n"
"            default_backend: \"portal\",\n"
"            routes: [{\n"
"                host: \"orders.internal\", path_prefix: "
"\"/orders.Orders/\",\n"
"                backend: \"orders\", firewall: false,\n"
"            }],\n"
"        } },\n"
"        backends: {\n"
"            portal: { servers: [\"10.0.0.10:8080\"] },\n"
"            orders: { http_version: \"2\", servers: [service(\"rpc1\", "
"\"10.0.0.11:50051\")] },\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"fn service(name: Text, address: Text) -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return { name: name, addr: address }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return {\n"
"        global: { acme: { storage: \"certificates\", directory: "
"\"letsencrypt-staging\" } },\n"
"        http: { surface: \"shield\" },\n"
"        frontends: { https: {\n"
"            binds: [\"0.0.0.0:443\"],\n"
"            tls: { auto: [\"portal.example.org\", \"orders.internal\"], "
"http3: true },\n"
"            default_backend: \"portal\",\n"
"            routes: [{\n"
"                host: \"orders.internal\", path_prefix: "
"\"/orders.Orders/\",\n"
"                backend: \"orders\", firewall: false,\n"
"            }],\n"
"        } },\n"
"        backends: {\n"
"            portal: { servers: [\"10.0.0.10:8080\"] },\n"
"            orders: { http_version: \"2\", servers: [service(\"rpc1\", "
"\"10.0.0.11:50051\")] },\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:179
msgid ""
"We replace the example names and addresses before deployment. For a "
"public name the ACME authority must be able to validate our domain. For "
"``orders.internal`` Sibuna issues and renews the certificate locally. We "
"install the local root certificate in each client's trust store."
msgstr ""
"Sustituimos los nombres y las direcciones del ejemplo antes de desplegar. "
"Para un nombre público, la autoridad ACME debe poder validar nuestro "
"dominio. Para ``orders.internal``, Sibuna emite y renueva el certificado "
"localmente. Instalamos el certificado raíz local en el almacén de "
"confianza de cada cliente."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:181
msgid ""
"Browsers can negotiate HTTP/2 over TCP or HTTP/3 over UDP on port 443. "
"The portal pool uses the default HTTP/1.1 upstream. The orders pool "
"selects HTTP/2 for gRPC trailers and streaming. For a public deployment "
"we change the staging directory to ``\"letsencrypt\"`` after testing "
"issuance. With an existing PEM bundle we replace ``auto`` with ``crt: "
"\"portal.pem\"`` and supply the certificates and private keys for the "
"names we serve."
msgstr ""
"Los navegadores pueden negociar HTTP/2 sobre TCP o HTTP/3 sobre UDP en el "
"puerto 443. El grupo del portal usa HTTP/1.1 por defecto hacia el origen. "
"El grupo de pedidos usa HTTP/2 para las cabeceras finales y los flujos de "
"gRPC. Después de probar la emisión, cambiamos el directorio de pruebas "
"por ``\"letsencrypt\"`` para el despliegue público. Con un paquete PEM "
"existente, sustituimos ``auto`` por ``crt: \"portal.pem\"`` y "
"proporcionamos los certificados y las claves privadas de los nombres que "
"servimos."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:183
msgid "Relay a TCP service"
msgstr "Retransmitir un servicio TCP"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:186
msgid ""
"Some clients speak a protocol of their own. We give the frontend and its "
"pool the same protocol. This complete module relays a connection to one "
"of two timetable feeds. The frontend limits new connections per source "
"and the pool checks whether each feed accepts TCP connections."
msgstr ""
"Algunos clientes hablan un protocolo propio. Damos al frontend y a su "
"grupo el mismo protocolo. Este módulo completo retransmite cada conexión "
"a una de dos fuentes de horarios. El frontend limita las conexiones "
"nuevas por origen y el grupo comprueba si cada fuente acepta conexiones "
"TCP."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:188
msgid ""
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return {\n"
"        frontends: { feed: {\n"
"            proto: \"tcp\", binds: [\"127.0.0.1:7000\"], default_backend: "
"\"feeds\",\n"
"            rate_limit: { conn_per_10s: 200 },\n"
"        } },\n"
"        backends: { feeds: {\n"
"            mode: \"tcp\", health_check: { kind: \"tcp\" },\n"
"            servers: [\"127.0.0.1:7001\", \"127.0.0.1:7002\"],\n"
"        } },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return {\n"
"        frontends: { feed: {\n"
"            proto: \"tcp\", binds: [\"127.0.0.1:7000\"], default_backend: "
"\"feeds\",\n"
"            rate_limit: { conn_per_10s: 200 },\n"
"        } },\n"
"        backends: { feeds: {\n"
"            mode: \"tcp\", health_check: { kind: \"tcp\" },\n"
"            servers: [\"127.0.0.1:7001\", \"127.0.0.1:7002\"],\n"
"        } },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:203
msgid "Share a UDP topology"
msgstr "Compartir una topología UDP"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:206
msgid ""
"Both nodes can use this module. In an empty directory we create mesh.key "
"with 32 random bytes and copy it securely to the other node. Each node "
"writes its own address and port from the nodes list into mesh.self. We "
"run the check in that directory. The shared key authenticates peers, and "
"accept_config lets them receive a cluster reload."
msgstr ""
"Ambos nodos pueden usar este módulo. En un directorio vacío creamos "
"mesh.key con 32 bytes aleatorios y lo copiamos de forma segura al otro "
"nodo. Cada nodo escribe en mesh.self su dirección y puerto de la lista "
"nodes. Ejecutamos la validación en ese directorio. La clave compartida "
"autentica a los pares y accept_config les permite recibir una recarga del "
"clúster."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:208
msgid ""
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    let peers = [\"10.20.0.11\", \"10.20.0.12\"]\n"
"    return {\n"
"        global: { admin_socket: \"edge.sock\", sticky_entries: 8192 },\n"
"        spill: { path: \"dns.spill\", size: \"1m\" },\n"
"        mesh: {\n"
"            nodes: [for peer in peers: \"${peer}:7946\"],\n"
"            self_file: \"mesh.self\",\n"
"            key_file: \"mesh.key\",\n"
"            accept_config: true, forward: {},\n"
"        },\n"
"        frontends: { dns: {\n"
"            proto: \"udp\", binds: [\"127.0.0.1:15353\"], "
"default_backend: \"resolvers\",\n"
"            udp_defense: { mode: \"rate_limit\", threshold_pps: 200 },\n"
"        } },\n"
"        backends: { resolvers: {\n"
"            mode: \"udp\", sticky: \"table\", max_flows_scope: "
"\"fleet\",\n"
"            servers: [\n"
"                { name: \"east\", addr: \"10.20.0.53:53\", max_flows: 300 "
"},\n"
"                { name: \"west\", addr: \"10.20.0.54:53\", max_flows: 300 "
"},\n"
"            ],\n"
"        } },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    let peers = [\"10.20.0.11\", \"10.20.0.12\"]\n"
"    return {\n"
"        global: { admin_socket: \"edge.sock\", sticky_entries: 8192 },\n"
"        spill: { path: \"dns.spill\", size: \"1m\" },\n"
"        mesh: {\n"
"            nodes: [for peer in peers: \"${peer}:7946\"],\n"
"            self_file: \"mesh.self\",\n"
"            key_file: \"mesh.key\",\n"
"            accept_config: true, forward: {},\n"
"        },\n"
"        frontends: { dns: {\n"
"            proto: \"udp\", binds: [\"127.0.0.1:15353\"], "
"default_backend: \"resolvers\",\n"
"            udp_defense: { mode: \"rate_limit\", threshold_pps: 200 },\n"
"        } },\n"
"        backends: { resolvers: {\n"
"            mode: \"udp\", sticky: \"table\", max_flows_scope: "
"\"fleet\",\n"
"            servers: [\n"
"                { name: \"east\", addr: \"10.20.0.53:53\", max_flows: 300 "
"},\n"
"                { name: \"west\", addr: \"10.20.0.54:53\", max_flows: 300 "
"},\n"
"            ],\n"
"        } },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:235
msgid ""
"We run the first command on one node only. On the second node we use the "
"same key and put 10.20.0.12:7946 in mesh.self. Each DNS listener serves "
"clients on its own loopback interface."
msgstr ""
"Ejecutamos el primer comando en un solo nodo. En el segundo usamos la "
"misma clave y escribimos 10.20.0.12:7946 en mesh.self. Cada nodo atiende "
"a los clientes DNS en su interfaz de bucle local."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:237
msgid ""
"(umask 077 && openssl rand 32 > mesh.key)\n"
"printf '%s\\n' '10.20.0.11:7946' > mesh.self"
msgstr ""
"(umask 077 && openssl rand 32 > mesh.key)\n"
"printf '%s\\n' '10.20.0.11:7946' > mesh.self"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:242
msgid ""
"The pool remembers a client's resolver. Each node keeps its own spill "
"file for recovering choices after a restart. The mesh shares choices and "
"the per-server flow allowance. We allow UDP port 7946 and the forwarding "
"port 7947 (TCP and UDP) between peers. After starting both nodes we can "
"compare their revisions with ``sibuna ctl edge.sock show cluster``."
msgstr ""
"El grupo recuerda el resolvedor de cada cliente. Cada nodo mantiene su "
"propio archivo de respaldo para recuperar las asignaciones tras un "
"reinicio. La malla comparte las asignaciones y el cupo de flujos por "
"servidor. Entre pares abrimos el puerto UDP 7946 y el puerto de reenvío "
"7947 (TCP y UDP). Tras arrancar ambos nodos podemos comparar sus "
"revisiones con ``sibuna ctl edge.sock show cluster``."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:244
msgid "Publish routes from a database"
msgstr "Publicar rutas desde una base de datos"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:247
msgid ""
"For a versioned topology we keep two modules. We use the first timetable "
"example as ``edge.jlv``. Its ``frontends``, ``backends`` and ``http`` are "
"the published revision. We save the following host settings as "
"``node.jlv``. The bind override lets this node serve the published web "
"frontend on port 8180."
msgstr ""
"Para versionar la topología mantenemos dos módulos. Usamos el primer "
"ejemplo de horarios como ``edge.jlv``. Sus secciones ``frontends``, "
"``backends`` y ``http`` forman la revisión publicada. Guardamos los "
"ajustes de la máquina que siguen como ``node.jlv``. Al sustituir la "
"dirección de escucha, este nodo sirve el frontend web publicado en el "
"puerto 8180."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:249
msgid ""
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return {\n"
"        global: { admin_socket: \"edge.sock\" },\n"
"        authority: {\n"
"            sqlite: \"authority.db\", node: \"station-1\", poll: \"5s\",\n"
"            cache: \"authority.cache\", binds: { web: "
"[\"127.0.0.1:8180\"] },\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"fn edge() -> Map<Value> {\n"
"    return {\n"
"        global: { admin_socket: \"edge.sock\" },\n"
"        authority: {\n"
"            sqlite: \"authority.db\", node: \"station-1\", poll: \"5s\",\n"
"            cache: \"authority.cache\", binds: { web: "
"[\"127.0.0.1:8180\"] },\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:261
msgid ""
"sibuna authority apply -c node.jlv -f edge.jlv --expect 0 --note \"first "
"timetable\"\n"
"sibuna authority history -c node.jlv\n"
"sibuna --config-file node.jlv"
msgstr ""
"sibuna authority apply -c node.jlv -f edge.jlv --expect 0 --note \"first "
"timetable\"\n"
"sibuna authority history -c node.jlv\n"
"sibuna --config-file node.jlv"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:267
msgid ""
"This example uses a build with SQLite support. We use revision zero only "
"for a new database. Before the next change we run ``sibuna authority diff "
"-c node.jlv -f edge.jlv`` and apply against the revision we reviewed. "
"SQLite serves one host. With PostgreSQL support we can serve a fleet. We "
"replace ``sqlite`` with ``postgres_url_file`` pointing to a protected "
"file containing the PostgreSQL connection URL. Each host supplies its own "
"node name and bind overrides."
msgstr ""
"Este ejemplo usa una compilación con SQLite. Usamos la revisión cero solo "
"para una base de datos nueva. Antes del siguiente cambio ejecutamos "
"``sibuna authority diff -c node.jlv -f edge.jlv`` y aplicamos el cambio "
"sobre la revisión examinada. SQLite sirve a una máquina. Con PostgreSQL "
"podemos servir a un conjunto de máquinas. Sustituimos ``sqlite`` por "
"``postgres_url_file``, que apunta a un archivo protegido con la URL de "
"conexión a PostgreSQL. Cada máquina aporta su nombre de nodo y sus "
"direcciones de escucha locales."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:269
msgid "Evaluation and diagnostics"
msgstr "Evaluación y diagnóstico"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:272
msgid ""
"Sibuna exposes the pure ``jlv.std.foundation`` library. Helpers live in "
"the same module. Deployment resources, filesystem operations and imports "
"from neighbouring files are outside this interface. Source and resulting "
"JSON each have a 256 KiB limit. Evaluation has a budget of one million "
"steps."
msgstr ""
"Sibuna ofrece la biblioteca pura ``jlv.std.foundation``. Las funciones "
"auxiliares viven en el mismo módulo. Los recursos de despliegue, el "
"acceso al sistema de archivos y las importaciones de archivos vecinos "
"quedan fuera de esta interfaz. El código y el JSON resultante tienen un "
"límite de 256 KiB cada uno. La evaluación admite un millón de pasos."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:274
msgid ""
"If the compiler reports an unknown name, we check its spelling and type "
"at the reported line and column. If validation reports an unknown "
"backend, we check that the route names a pool in the returned map. A "
"rejected reload keeps the previous routing configuration."
msgstr ""
"Si el compilador indica un nombre desconocido, revisamos la grafía y el "
"tipo en la línea y columna indicadas. Si la validación informa de un "
"backend desconocido, comprobamos que la ruta nombre un grupo del mapa "
"devuelto. Si se rechaza la recarga, sigue activa la configuración "
"anterior."

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:276
msgid "Where to configure each part"
msgstr "Dónde configuramos cada componente"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/jlavi.rst:279
msgid ""
"The following sections give the supported options, defaults and restart "
"rules. A map in an operations example belongs at the same position in the "
"value returned by ``edge()``. A quoted JSON field such as "
"``\"max_flows\": 4096`` can be written as ``max_flows: 4096`` in Jlavi."
msgstr ""
"Las siguientes secciones dan las opciones admitidas, los valores "
"predeterminados y las reglas de reinicio. Un mapa de un ejemplo de "
"operaciones ocupa el mismo lugar en el valor que devuelve ``edge()``. Un "
"campo JSON como ``\"max_flows\": 4096`` se puede escribir en Jlavi como "
"``max_flows: 4096``."

